     "text": "Kim-Taylor Clinic\nRe: Robert Kelley (DOB 07/14/1959)\n\nDr. Cody Butler\nAddiction Medicine\nKim-Taylor Clinic\n\nDate: January 15, 2026\n\nTo Whom It May Concern,\n\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive medical summary of Mr. Robert Kelley, a 66-year-old male under my care since 2014 for his Alcohol use disorder, currently in a treated and controlled state.\n\nMr. Kelley was last seen on December 30, 2025, for a follow-up visit regarding his Alcohol use disorder. At the time of the visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 140/79 mmHg, and he weighed 212 pounds. Despite his longstanding abstinence of 11.3 years, he has been non-compliant with his prescribed medication, naltrexone 50 mg, and has missed several follow-up appointments. His Alcohol use disorder has been managed through Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) treatment, and he has not experienced any relapses.\n\nOn March 25, 2025, Mr. Kelley was seen for a routine check-up related to his Alcohol use disorder, showing a blood pressure of 141/86 mmHg and weighing 214 pounds. He reported doing well at that time.\n\nFurther back, on June 18, 2024, he visited for a back strain. His blood pressure was 144/90 mmHg, and his weight was 213 pounds. It was noted that he continues suffer from Alcohol use disorder, with his treatment history remaining consistent at 11.3 years\n"
    }
